d do not refetch/poll. An unresolved thread can be historical: inspect `outdated`, current code/commit, and addressed markers. [Task 1]\n   205\t- Related skill: `skills/thread-aware-pr-review-triage/SKILL.md`. [Task 1]\n   328\t### rollout_summary_files\n   329\t\n   330\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T04:09:11+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, DATA-1 published; AUTH-1 has one unresolved remote FastAPI CI failure)\n   331\t\n   332\t### keywords\n   333\t\n   334\t- DATA-1, AUTH-1, canonical-gateway, origin/dev, 72aabce, placement, CAS, HMAC assertions, replay protection, single-writer-strong, PR #121, PR #120, FastAPI, StopIteration\n   335\t\n   336\t## User preferences\n   337\t\n   338\t- when the user requests new worktrees “off `origin/dev`” -> preserve the dirty checkout, create an isolated worktree from the authoritative exact ref, and keep requested scopes separate. [Task 1]\n   339\t- when the user requests end-to-end work in new worktrees -> preserve the dirty checkout, use freshly fetched `origin/dev` worktrees, and carry publication/verification through only when authorized. [Task 1]\n   340\t\n   341\t## Reusable knowledge\n   342\t\n   343\t- DATA-1 PR #121 at `049cfc3e` covers placement/CAS ownership, signed gateway assertions, pre-execution fencing, sync/WebSocket paths, migration fencing, observability, adapters, and docs. AUTH-1 PR #120 at `be0dde5d` covers identity placement/CAS, HMAC assertions with nonce replay protection, direct/gateway modes, TypeScript/Python adapters, Swift, and docs. [Task 1]\n   344\t- DynamoDB placement requires `consistencyModel: 'single-writer-strong'` and consistent reads; Global Table replicas are not globally atomic. Local validation passed, but Redis/DO/cross-region/provider/KMS/nonce/failover/O