0.1` was retrieved and followed. Both issues were read in full, including linked architecture/rationale documents and comments. The original dirty `superfunctions-dev` checkout was preserved.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Task 1: DATA-1 DataFn canonical-gateway routing\n    12\t\n    13\tOutcome: success\n    14\t\n    15\tKey steps:\n    16\t- Fetched `origin/dev` at `72aabce915426325450663feffd7a53089ef4489` and created detached worktree `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/DATA-1`.\n    17\t- Implemented tenant placement, atomic claims/CAS epoch moves, gateway dispatch, signed assertions, bounded retry, pre-execution fencing, sync/WebSocket handling, migration coordination, observability, provider-neutral adapters, tests, and documentation.\n    18\t- Applied exactly one consolidated PR-review remediation round.\n    19\t- Committed and pushed final head `049cfc3e92e4c77f2dc3c996b205e57ca8a734f7` to branch `DATA-1`; opened PR #121 targeting `dev`.\n    20\t- Verified clean worktree, matching local/remote/PR heads, mergeability, focused tests, DataFn suites, typecheck/build/docs, and green or skipped remote checks.\n    21\t\n    22\tReusable knowledge:\n    23\t- DATA-1’s placement directory must remain separate from the permission-grant projection; permission indexing must never determine namespace ownership.\n    24\t- Routing assertions bind request identity and body/path data, and stale routing may be retried only once before execution.\n    25\t- The original checkout contained unrelated untracked `.conduct` artifacts and must not be cleaned or modified.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Task 2: AUTH-1 AuthFn canonical-gateway routing\n    28\t\n    29\tOutcome: partial\n    30\t\n    31\tKey steps:\n    32\t- Created detached worktree `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/AUTH-1` from the same `origin/dev` base.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0399f-ce6e-7d31-bfc8-f5b6e4f126f5","create_time":1787673783.693687}}}
