*Deletion fencing**: Added a durable `deleting` placement state, pre-cascade fencing, failure restoration, fail-closed finalization, and explicit operator repair helpers.\\n- **Routing hardening**: Retained replay claims through accepted clock skew, rejected `deleting` placements before execution, and marked transport failures as indeterminate.\\n- **Runtime parity**: Allowed Python gateway cells without a configured-region catalog while preserving unknown-cell validation for non-empty catalogs.\\n- **Provider and observability fixes**: Pinned internally constructed DynamoDB placement clients to the writer region and preserved canonical `errorCode` metadata while redacting secret-like fields.\\n- **Compatibility updates**: Restored Python runtime/environment route aliases, preserved raw query bytes in URL-less requests, and bumped the shared Python adapter package versions.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against d7f6446;\\nif commits have landed on AUTH-1 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 56\\n- Commits reviewed: 1\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: AUTH-1 (d7f6446)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - d7f6446 — AUTH-1: harden canonical gateway review edge cases\\n- Prior pullfrog review: a168fa1 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5007081386)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/120?action=fix&review_id=5008