s/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004494499\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/120\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004494499\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/120\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T04:16:05Z\",\"commit_id\":\"be0dde5d0b2fc65c877f304ff68feb0e0717013a\"},{\"id\":5004498941,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABKkqX_Q\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1768019?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/pullfrog\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pullfrog%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> Tombstoning before a non-transactional deletion can make a surviving account permanently unreachable after a transient delete failure.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** Reviewed the `be0dde5` delta since the Pullfrog review written against `e763ea9`.\\n\\n- **Cell enforcement**: Executed Python route middleware in FastAPI and Flask before handlers, preserving request URL and query data through buffering.\\n- **Placement lifecycle**: Resumed target or source service before publishing active ownership and retained the `moving` fence when recovery fails.\\n- **Deletion fencing**: Required canonical identity-key derivation and moved placement tombstoning into the fail-closed pre-delete hook.\\n- **Routing hardening**: Bounded placement caches, added mismatch clock-skew handling, validated stored placements, and tightened canonical runtime behavior.\\n- **Provider and contract checks**: Enforced a declared DynamoDB writer region and expanded adapter assertions, event/error documentation, and focused parity tests.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against be0dde5;\\nif commits have landed on AUTH-1 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 44\\n- Commits reviewed: 3\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: AUTH-1 (be0dde5)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - be0dde5 — AUTH-1: address gateway review findings\\n  - e763ea9 — AUTH-1: satisfy full Python typecheck\\n  - 6641e95 — AUTH-1: add canonical gateway identity routing\\n- Prior pullfrog review: e763ea9 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004271614)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-white-full-18px.png\\\"><img src=\\\"https://pullfrog.com/logos/frog-green-full-18px.png\\\" width=\\\"9px\\\" height=\\\"9px\\\" style=\\\"vertical-align: middle; \\\" alt=\\\"Pullfrog\\\"></picture></a>&nbsp;&nbsp;｜ [Fix all ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/120?action=fix&review_id=5004498941) ｜ [Fix 👍s ➔](https://pullfrog.com/trigger/21nCo/super-functions/120?action=fix-approved&review_id=5004498941) ｜ [View workflow run](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32688737622/job/97318451821) ｜ Using `GPT Sol` ｜ [𝕏](https://x.com/pullfrogai)</sup>\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004498941\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/120\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004498941\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/120\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T04:17:24Z\",\"commit_id\":\"be0dde5d0b2fc65c877f304ff68feb0e0717013a\"},{\"id\":5004543327,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABKktFXw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\"id\":191113872,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDOC2QqkA\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1082092?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/cubic-dev-ai\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**3 issues found** across 31 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"authfn/docs/content/docs/reference/events.md\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"authfn/docs/content/docs/reference/events.md:50\\\">\\nP3: The Outcome column claims `success` for `authfn.routing.placement_claimed`, `forwarded`, and `retry`, but their only emission sites (gateway-routing.ts:359, 418, 451) pass metadata without an `outcome` key, and `emit()` sets `outcome` to `undefined` unless `metadata.outcome` is a string. Align the two: either add `outcome: 'success'` to those three emit calls (and an explicit outcome at the gateway `mismatch`/`cell_unavailable` sites), or drop these Outcome claims from the docs.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"authfn/swift/Sources/AuthFnClient/AuthFnClient.swift\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"authfn/swift/Sources/AuthFnClient/AuthFnClient.swift:25\\\">\\nP2: When this client talks to the Python authfn kernel, `runtime()` now requests `/auth/environment`, but Python exposes only `/auth/runtime`, so the call returns a route-not-found error. Expose `/environment` in the Python kernel before switching this client, or retain a compatibility fallback.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"authfn/core/src/core/regions.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"authfn/core/src/core/regions.ts:502\\\">\\nP2: The `authfn.region.lookup` event emitted when the gateway lookup projection fails always contains `errorCode: '[redacted]'` instead of the real error code. `sanitizeEvent` redacts any metadata key matching `/...|code|.../i`, and the key `errorCode` matches (even `failureCode` or `statusCode` would). Because the catch block swallows the error and only this event signals the failure, the projected write failure is effectively silent — `readErrorCode` adds no diagnostic value. Rename the metadata key to one without the `code` substring, e.g. `errorType` or `errorName`.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/120/ai_pr_review_1787544347845_637d746a-481b-4210-86b4-cbd43a938492?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F120)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787544347845_637d746a-481b-4210-86b4-cbd43a938492:be0dde5d0b2fc65c877f304ff68feb0e0717013a:65d0c00e-ac9f-4d6d-bc43-210b13557cce -->\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004543327\",\"pull_request_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/120\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"_links\":{\"html\":{\"href\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5004543327\"},\"pull_request\":{\"href\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/21nCo/super-functions/pulls/120\"}},\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T04:28:54Z\",\"commit_id\":\"be0dde5d0b2fc65c877f304ff68feb0e0717013a\"},{\"id\":5007062399,\"node_id\":\"PRR_kwDOP-e7KM8AAAABKnG1fw\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"id\":226033991,\"node_id\":\"BOT_kgDODXkBRw\",\"avatar_url\":\"https:/