bd60a1` delta since the prior Pullfrog review against `d7f6446`.\\n\\n- **Moved deletion cleanup around the full failure window**: Included the composed before-delete hook chain so later hook rejection restores the durable placement fence.\\n- **Bound deletion to the verified routed identity**: Exposed the cell-validated identity key during request execution and preferred it over an email-derived key for fencing, restoration, and finalization.\\n- **Prevented TypeScript rollback after target resume**: Left placement fenced when target resume begins or target activation loses its CAS race.\\n- **Strengthened replay and provider coverage**: Proved routed assertion replay rejection and verified internally constructed DynamoDB clients use the declared writer region with consistent reads.\\n- **Aligned supporting contracts**: Preserved Python `errorCode` observability metadata, made placement protocol stubs explicit, and documented placement errors as retryable.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 2bd60a1;\\nif commits have landed on AUTH-1 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting on it.\\n\\n- Mode: IncrementalReview (delta against prior pullfrog review)\\n- Files reviewed: 60\\n- Commits reviewed: 6\\n- Base: dev (72aabce)\\n- Head: AUTH-1 (2bd60a1)\\n- Reviewed commits:\\n  - 2bd60a17 — fix(authfn): address latest AUTH-1 review findings\\n  - d7f6446f — AUTH-1: harden canonical gateway review edge cases\\n  - a168fa1a — fix(authfn): address PR review findings\\n  - be0dde5d — AUTH-1: address gateway review findings\\n  - e763ea93 — AUTH-1: satisfy full Python typecheck\\n  - 6641e951 — AUTH-1: add canonical gateway identity routing\\n- Prior pullfrog review: d7f6446 (https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5008849195)\\n-->\\n\\n<!-- PULLFROG_DIVIDER_DO_NOT_REMOVE_PLZ -->\\n<sup><a href=\\\"https://pullfrog.com\\\"><picture><source media=\\\