ved_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**2 issues found** across 11 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"authfn/docs/content/docs/recipes/canonical-gateway-multi-region.md\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"authfn/docs/content/docs/recipes/canonical-gateway-multi-region.md:110\\\">\\nP2: When an admin authorizer returns `true` or omits `actorId`, the documented administrator path does not use `identityKeyForUserId`: deletion defaults the actor to the target user and falls back to the session/email key. Require a distinct admin `actorId` for this routing contract, or qualify the table entry and explain the requirement.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"authfn/core/src/core/gateway-routing.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"authfn/core/src/core/gateway-routing.ts:744\\\">\\nP1: When two account deletions overlap, this returns the shared `deleting` fence and lets both cascades run. If one fails, its failure hook can restore `active` while the other finishes deleting, leaving the deleted account routable as active. Serialize deletion attempts or bind the fence to an operation token so only the owning attempt can reuse it.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/120/ai_pr_review_1787658457424_788f5450-e6d4-448b-96c1-1efda35686a4?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.