om/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/cubic-dev-ai%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:v=feddacbe-9604-4aad-b6da-1831e465ca24 -->\\n<!-- cubic:review-run=ab5b887c-c3ef-4cdc-a261-fa55f1dff861 -->\\n<!-- metadata:{\\\"confidence\\\":9} -->\\nP2: When an administrator deletes a user by ID who has no primary email, this delegated branch discards the routed identity and leaves no target placement key, so the deletion is rejected before any database work. Add a target-user-ID placement-key path and use it consistently for fencing, finalization, and rollback.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents</summary>\\n\\n```text\\nCheck if this issue is valid — if so, understand the root cause and fix it. At authfn/multi-region/src/index.ts, line 405:\\n\\n<comment>When an administrator deletes a user by ID who has no primary email, this delegated branch discards the routed identity and leaves no target placement key, so the deletion is rejected before any database work. Add a target-user-ID placement-key path and use it consistently for fencing, finalization, and rollback.</comment>\\n\\n<file context>\\n@@ -377,11 +396,16 @@ function readOptionalString(value: unknown): string | undefined {\\n-  const verifiedIdentityKey = authFnVerifiedRoutingIdentityKey(request);\\n-  if (verifiedIdentityKey) return verifiedIdentityKey;\\n+  const delegatedDelete = Boolean(actorId && targetUserId && actorId !== targetUserId);\\n+  if (!delegatedDelete) {\\n+    const verifiedIdentityKey = authFnVerifiedRoutingIdentityKey(request);\\n+    if (verifiedIdentityKey) return verifiedIdentityKey;\\n</file context>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n✅ Addressed in [`862575f`](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/commit/862575f1db467cbc65e0e9ca52349908392863e6)\",\"created_at\":\