/static/llms-full.txt:2072:- [Runtime](./runtime) — per-request overlays.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:2707:- [Runtime resolver](./runtime) — per-request issuer, base URL, OAuth, cookie domain.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:3385:The placement directory is deliberately separate from the existing identifier lookup projection. Its atomic record is `{ identityKey, regionId, epoch, state }`; only `active` records execute. `moving` records fence writes and `tombstoned` records fail closed. Cell destinations are opaque values returned by the cell registry and are never stored in placement or sent publicly.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:3543:- [Runtime](./runtime) — how region overlays compose with `runtime.resolve`.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:3550:<!-- page:docs:core-concepts/runtime.md path:/docs/core-concepts/runtime -->\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:4153:- `GET /auth/environment` (per-region environment — region id, issuer, base URL, cookie policy).\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:6052:| `GET` | `/auth/environment` | `getEnvironment` | Returns the resolved request environment: `{ regionId, issuer, baseUrl, … }`. |\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:6070:The matched region's overlays (`cookie`, `oauth`, `issuer`, `baseUrl`) are applied on top of the base runtime. See [Concepts → Runtime](../core-concepts/runtime) for how this composes with the user-supplied resolver.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:6120:- [Concepts → Runtime](../core-concepts/runtime)\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:8165:    identityKeyForIdentifier: identityKeys.fromEmail,\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:8213:| Account deletion and email change | Route. | Verified session handle for self-service; `identityKeyForUserId` for an administrator's target, independent of whether the admin authorizer supplies an `actorId`. | Validate routing before mutation. Account deletion CAS-fences `active` to durable `deleting` before the cascade, restores `active` if the cascade fails, and publishes `tombstoned` only after success. A second deletion attempt is rejected while that fence exists, preventing concurrent cascades from restoring or finalizing each other's state. After inspecting the cascade outcome, an operator may repair a stranded fence with `restoreAuthFnIdentityDeletion` or `finalizeAuthFnIdentityDeletion`; email-change flows must update placement with an application-level transaction/outbox protocol. |\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:8229:Invalidate gateway placement caches after every claim, move, tombstone, and operator repair. Old assertions are rejected by epoch even when their TTL has not elapsed.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:8236:- Missing/tombstoned established placement: fail closed. Do not enumerate the identity through the public lookup route.\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:9766:| `GET` | `/auth/environment` | `getEnvironment` | Resolved request environment — region id, issuer, base URL, and cookie policy. |\nauthfn/docs/static/llms-full.txt:10172:  getEnvironment(): Promise<…>;\npackages/python-core/superfunctions/http/__init__.py:13:from .executor import execute_route\npackages/python-core/superfunctions/http/__init__.py:63:    \"execute_route\",\npackages/python-core/superfunctions/http/executor.py:10:async def execute_route(\npackages/python-core/superfunctions/http/executor.py:18:    for middleware in reversed((route.middleware or []) if route else []):\npackages/python-core/superfunctions/http/executor.py:36:__all__ = [\"execute_route\"]\nauthfn/docs/content/docs/sdk/client.md:108:  getEnvironment(): Promise<…>;\nauthfn/docs/content/docs/reference/routes.md:22:| `GET` | `/auth/environment` | `getEnvironment` | Resolved request environment — region id, issuer, base URL, and cookie policy. |\nauthfn/docs/content/docs/core-concepts/regions.md:19:The placement directory is deliberately separate from the existing identifier lookup projection. Its atomic record is `{ identityKey, regionId, epoch, state }`; only `activ