{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T16:10:46.010Z","ordinal":11879,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0eef853664611d0c016a8dbe847e4487d09c3fa92f158a0eeb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_0tT0hntWwvXi0wprDdmR0Wqt","name":"exec","input":"const reviews=load(\"auth1r4_reviews\");\nconst nonempty=reviews.filter(r=>r.body && r.body.trim()).sort((a,b)=>String(a.submitted_at).localeCompare(String(b.submitted_at)));\nfor (const r of nonempty.slice(-18)) {\n  text(JSON.stringify({\n    id:r.id,user:r.user?.login,state:r.state,submitted_at:r.submitted_at,\n    commit_id:r.commit_id,html_url:r.html_url,body:r.body\n  }));\n}\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a039ae-961d-7fa0-92b9-1975e7915734","create_time":1787674234.600591}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T16:10:46.048Z","ordinal":11880,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a039b0-3ba0-7e52-8dce-3d89a4a7eb95","call_id":"call_0tT0hntWwvXi0wprDdmR0Wqt","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10594)\nTotal output lines: 18\n\n{\"id\":5008861540,\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T14:21:04Z\",\"commit_id\":\"d7f6446f6bee158d76ce05df07e7098b53e8b6e1\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5008861540\",\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**2 issues found** across 25 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\\n\\n```text\\n\\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\\n\\n\\n<file name=\\\"authfn/core/src/core/observability.ts\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"authfn/core/src/core/observability.ts:33\\\">\\nP2: When the same failure is emitted by Python, `metadata.errorCode` is still redacted while TypeScript now preserves it. Update the Python sanitizer and parity tests so the documented error-code field behaves consistently across runtimes.</violation>\\n</file>\\n\\n<file name=\\\"packages/python-core/pyproject.toml\\\">\\n\\n<violation number=\\\"1\\\" location=\\\"packages/python-core/pyproject.toml:7\\\">\\nP2: This bump leaves the public `superfunctions.__version__` at `0.1.0` while packaging metadata reports `0.1.1`. Update the runtime version constant with the package metadata so version checks and diagnostics agree.</violation>\\n</file>\\n```\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/120/ai_pr_review_1787580802541_7908a94b-7e2f-4468-ba4f-e95ba5adea9e?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F120)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787580802541_7908a94b-7e2f-4468-ba4f-e95ba5adea9e:d7f6446f6bee158d76ce05df07e7098b53e8b6e1:294072f7-e40b-4ede-a85f-fa6c576b7595 -->\"}\n{\"id\":5010160701,\"user\":\"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T16:25:30Z\",\"commit_id\":\"2bd60a175d397267c276498dbb834c8f52bfc497\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5010160701\",\"body\":\"\\n### 💡 Codex Review\\n\\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\\n\\n**Reviewed commit:** `2bd60a175d`\\n    \\n\\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\\n<br/>\\n\\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\\n- Open a pull request for review\\n- Mark a draft as ready\\n- Comment \\\"@codex review\\\".\\n\\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR. Try commenting \\\"@codex address that feedback\\\".\\n            \\n</details>\"}\n{\"id\":5010173482,\"user\":\"cubic-dev-ai[bot]\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T16:26:48Z\",\"commit_id\":\"2bd60a175d397267c276498dbb834c8f52bfc497\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5010173482\",\"body\":\"<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\\n**All reported issues were addressed** across 13 files (changes from recent commits).\\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\\n\\n<sub>**Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/120/ai_pr_review_1787588417695_ed20b1c2-6702-42ce-911a-250281c3aea6?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F120)</sub>\\n\\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787588417695_ed20b1c2-6702-42ce-911a-250281c3aea6:2bd60a175d397267c276498dbb834c8f52bfc497:9eb977c5-417e-4076-adbf-38b609a6b99b -->\"}\n{\"id\":5010175317,\"user\":\"pullfrog[bot]\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-08-24T16:27:00Z\",\"commit_id\":\"2bd60a175d397267c276498dbb834c8f52bfc497\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120#pullrequestreview-5010175317\",\"body\":\"> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The Python identity-move path must preserve the same post-resume fence now enforced in TypeScript before this merges.\\n\\n**Reviewed changes** Reviewed the `2bd60a1` delta since the prior Pullfrog review against `d7f6446`.\\n\\n- **Moved deletion cleanup around the full failure window**: Included the composed before-delete hook chain so later hook rejection restores the durable placement fence.\\n- **Bound deletion to the verified routed identity**: Exposed the cell-validated identity key during request execution and preferred it over an email-derived key for fencing, restoration, and finalization.\\n- **Prevented TypeScript rollback after target resume**: Left placement fenced when target resume begins or target activation loses its CAS race.\\n- **Strengthened replay and provider coverage**: Proved routed assertion replay rejection and verified internally constructed DynamoDB clients use the declared writer region with consistent reads.\\n- **Aligned supporting contracts**: Preserved Python `errorCode` observability metadata, made placement protocol stubs explicit, and documented placement errors as retryable.\\n\\n<!--\\nPullfrog review met