{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T16:12:59.573Z","ordinal":11930,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a039b2-4534-74f2-a74a-d9b3a86d2ba0","call_id":"call_8E12ijxznyhjxAiaRC3Qv2On","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"2:scope: Use for independently replaying, reviewing, and delivering McpFn and UiFn changes from `sf-next/next` to `origin/dev` without disturbing a dirty checkout.\n17:- when the user asks for “2 separate PRs one for mcpfn and another for uifn into origin/dev from sf-next/next” -> preserve the dirty checkout, use separate clean worktrees from the authoritative refs, and keep scopes/allowlists independent. [Task 1]\n22:- Move UiFn generated `.conduct` verifier output outside the PR worktree before staging. A green release gate does not prove mergeability: PR #119 remained `DIRTY` from a pre-existing merge conflict. [Task 1]\n323:scope: Use for DATA-1/AUTH-1 local-only canonical-gateway implementation behind a hosted approval gate.\n324:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree, approval, and exact-head procedures are reusable, but code, PR, CI, and deployment evidence are snapshot-specific.\n326:## Task 1: Implement DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in isolated worktrees, partial\n330:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T04:09:11+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, DATA-1 published; AUTH-1 has one unresolved remote FastAPI CI failure)\n334:- DATA-1, AUTH-1, canonical-gateway, origin/dev, 72aabce, placement, CAS, HMAC assertions, replay protection, single-writer-strong, PR #121, PR #120, FastAPI, StopIteration\n338:- when the user requests new worktrees “off `origin/dev`” -> preserve the dirty checkout, create an isolated worktree from the authoritative exact ref, and keep requested scopes separate. [Task 1]\n339:- when the user requests end-to-end work in new worktrees -> preserve the dirty checkout, use freshly fetched `origin/dev` worktrees, and carry publication/verification through only when authorized. [Task 1]\n343:- DATA-1 PR #121 at `049cfc3e` covers placement/CAS ownership, signed gateway assertions, pre-execution fencing, sync/WebSocket paths, migration fencing, observability, adapters, and docs. AUTH-1 PR #120 at `be0dde5d` covers identity placement/CAS, HMAC assertions with nonce replay protection, direct/gateway modes, TypeScript/Python adapters, Swift, and docs. [Task 1]\n348:- Remote FastAPI CI on AUTH-1 failed with `StopIteration` locating `/api/auth/session`; the one-remediation-round limit meant it remained open. Do not call remote CI or live multi-region behavior verified from local success. [Task 1]\n350:# Task Group: August 22 DevFn PR #117 implementation and exact-head delivery\n351:scope: Use for hosted-skill-led DEV-1 work from `next`, review remediation in a dedicated PR-head worktree, and an authorized exact-head push.\n520:- For a live PR fix pass, refetch paginated GraphQL review threads plus reviews, issue comments, and inline comments; validate against the exact head, then merge with an exact-head guard. PR #48 merged to `next` at `523c66ae8cf981ff8331d56386cec1f81c704182`. [Task 1]\n969:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/12/rollout-2026-08-12T18-19-04-019ff604-e744-7f51-9e04-117871db75c4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-18T13:37:29+00:00, thread_id=019ff604-e744-7f51-9e04-117871db75c4, dirty-next preservation, current MDFN remediation, full verify:mdfn, PR #43 exact-head merge)\n1005:- For private Superfunctions PR operations, use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`; target `sf-next/next`, include `.conduct` for that target, verify ancestry/changed files/generated artifacts, and read back the exact live PR head. The final SFN-21 contract gate recorded 29 packages, 130 resources, 347 operations and 74/74 tests. [Task 3]\n1408:scope: Use for exact-head security/readiness audits, authorized package publishing, or branch/worktree inventory. Keep dirty sources isolated and distinguish local gates from external CI/deployment proof.\n1445:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SF-8-ci-fixes, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/11/rollout-2026-08-11T18-06-59-019ff0d3-7b1f-7e03-ab55-c5c5fd150841.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T12:58:28+00:00, thread_id=019ff0d3-7b1f-7e03-ab55-c5c5fd150841, reviewed fixes pushed and PR #103 merged with exact-head guard)\n1454:- preserve a dirty checkout and use an isolated exact-head worktree for audit/release work; “what do you think?” and “resume” requested review, not remediation. [Task 1]\n1456:- when the user asked for “splane PR fixes” -> retrieve the live hosted workflow, write/reconcile evidence before edits, and preserve an existing dirty PR checkout by using a dedicated exact-head worktree. Push only after explicit authorization and an exact-head remote guard. [Task 4]\n1460:- `sf-next/next`, not `origin/next`, is the valid next ref. In private 21n repos, use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` if default `gh` returns misleading 404. Test caller-supplied `environmentId` where IDs outrank environment scope. [Task 1]\n1462:- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\n1464:- For private Superfunctions PRs, inspect authenticated current `reviewThreads`/head comments, including `isResolved` and `isOutdated`, before editing. PR #103 used a clean isolated exact-head worktree because the existing checkout was dirty; after user authorization, fetch `origin/SF-8`, require it to equal `HEAD^`, then push `HEAD:SF-8` and verify local/remote/live PR SHA equality. [Task 4]\n1556:scope: Use for exact-head PR audits or authorized remediation in Superfunctions. Preserve dirty checkouts, retrieve current review surfaces, distinguish live CI blockers from code results, and verify post-push PR state.\n1563:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T19-20-11-019febf0-242e-7502-9f6f-34122b41d82c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T05:03:37+00:00, thread_id=019febf0-242e-7502-9f6f-34122b41d82c, PR #93 remediation, semantic conflict resolution, and merge into dev completed)\n1593:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/SF-8-ci-fixes, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/11/rollout-2026-08-11T18-06-59-019ff0d3-7b1f-7e03-ab55-c5c5fd150841.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T12:58:28+00:00, thread_id=019ff0d3-7b1f-7e03-ab55-c5c5fd150841, review evidence, exact-head push, and merged verification)\n1603:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/12/rollout-2026-08-12T18-19-04-019ff604-e744-7f51-9e04-117871db75c4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-18T13:37:29+00:00, thread_id=019ff604-e744-7f51-9e04-117871db75c4, current MDFN remediation, full verify:mdfn, PR #43 exact-head merge)\n1685:- PR #38 merged into `sf-next/next` at `12580dd2`. Base conflicts in `.conduct/logs.csv`, `README.md`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, and `release-packages.json` were resolved by retaining MailFn and McpFn registrations and regenerating the lockfile; GitHub operations used `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`. [Task 2]\n1987:- when the user said \"fix all merge conflicts\" and \"dont commit or push yet\" -> leave resolution local/uncommitted and do not cross the publication boundary. [Task 1]\n2350:applies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-SFN-15-uifn; reuse_rule=recheck the dirty checkout, current supported-framework scope, evidence paths, disk capacity, and release state before reuse.\n3276:- router-manual-acquisition, Product Hunt, CDP PNG, cdp-png-capture.mjs, review_ready, workflow validation, R2, Postgres, Cloudflare Worker, packages/core/src/cloudflare.ts, gh-other\n3915:## Task 15: Resolve PR #748 merge conflicts locally and leave the merge pending, success\n3932:- when the user says “fix the merge conflict - dont commit or push yet” -> resolve locally, stage the merge result, and leave the repository in its pending-merge state without creating a commit or push. [Task 11]\n5489:- when the user asks to \"explain the merge conflicts\" before a fix -> start with a grounded conflict explanation and resolution plan before editing. [Task 28]\n5544:- Symptom: a merge conflict in Drizzle metadata is treated like a broad code conflict. Cause: the journal collision is not isolated from the feature changes. Fix: inspect `drizzle/meta/_journal.json`, renumber the migration cleanly, and validate with `drizzle-kit check`. [Task 5]\n{\"baseRefName\":\"dev\",\"headRefName\":\"AUTH-1\",\"headRefOid\":\"bf3a19d192741f0ef19c676cb37e7713a1794aaa\",\"isDraft\":false,\"mergeStateStatus\":\"UNSTABLE\",\"mergeable\":\"MERGEABLE\",\"number\":120,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-08-25T15:42:27Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/actions/runs/32867431534/job/97866034121\",\"name\":\"Plan\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-25T15:42:14Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-08-25T15:44:25Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/21nCo/super-f