{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T16:15:32.947Z","ordinal":12023,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a039b1-ee94-7a32-9b14-cbd38fac0e1c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-433e15b8-55ee-4752-a809-35e419197ee8","process_id":"99722","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '323,344p;516,522p;1001,1007p;1458,1465p'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '323,344p;516,522p;1001,1007p;1458,1465p'","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"   323\tscope: Use for DATA-1/AUTH-1 local-only canonical-gateway implementation behind a hosted approval gate.\n   324\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree, approval, and exact-head procedures are reusable, but code, PR, CI, and deployment evidence are snapshot-specific.\n   325\t\n   326\t## Task 1: Implement DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in isolated worktrees, partial\n   327\t\n   328\t### rollout_summary_files\n   329\t\n   330\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T04:09:11+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, DATA-1 published; AUTH-1 has one unresolved remote FastAPI CI failure)\n   331\t\n   332\t### keywords\n   333\t\n   334\t- DATA-1, AUTH-1, canonical-gateway, origin/dev, 72aabce, placement, CAS, HMAC assertions, replay protection, single-writer-strong, PR #121, PR #120, FastAPI, StopIteration\n   335\t\n   336\t## User preferences\n   337\t\n   338\t- when the user requests new worktrees “off `origin/dev`” -> preserve the dirty checkout, create an isolated worktree from the authoritative exact ref, and keep requested scopes separate. [Task 1]\n   339\t- when the user requests end-to-end work in new worktrees -> preserve the dirty checkout, use freshly fetched `origin/dev` worktrees, and carry publication/verification through only when authorized. [Task 1]\n   340\t\n   341\t## Reusable knowledge\n   342\t\n   343\t- DATA-1 PR #121 at `049cfc3e` covers placement/CAS ownership, signed gateway assertions, pre-execution fencing, sync/WebSocket paths, migration fencing, observability, adapters, and docs. AUTH-1 PR #120 at `be0dde5d` covers identity placement/CAS, HMAC assertions with nonce replay protection, direct/gateway modes, TypeScript/Python adapters, Swift, and docs. [Task 1]\n   344\t- DynamoDB placement requires `consistencyModel: 'single-writer-strong'` and consistent reads; Global Table replicas are not globally atomic. Local validation passed, but Redis/DO/cross-region/provider/KMS/nonce/failover/OAuth proof was not performed. [Task 1]\n   516\t\n   517\t## Reusable knowledge\n   518\t\n   519\t- Super Console needs manifest-driven presentation/query/parent metadata, generic contextual navigation, action-input binding, and generic filter mapping; native selects violate the UI surface guard and should use the UIFn select compound. [Task 1]\n   520\t- For a live PR fix pass, refetch paginated GraphQL review threads plus reviews, issue comments, and inline comments; validate against the exact head, then merge with an exact-head guard. PR #48 merged to `next` at `523c66ae8cf981ff8331d56386cec1f81c704182`. [Task 1]\n   521\t- Safely synchronize with `git fetch sf-next next`, ancestry check, `git switch next`, `git merge --ff-only sf-next/next`, local-branch deletion, upstream reset, and `git rev-list --left-right --count next...sf-next/next`; preserve the separate `superfunctions-dev` worktree. [Task 1]\n   522\t\n  1001\t\n  1002\t- `sf-next/next` is the source branch; preserve from the pre-sync local `next` commit, compare fingerprints/untracked hashes, then `git pull --ff-only sf-next next`. MDFN keeps Markdown canonical behind core → DOM → adapter-kit → React/Svelte/Solid; read-only keymaps/transactions must be gated, visual positions mapped to Markdown offsets, and destructive compaction must require `compact-collaboration`, not ordinary `collaborate`. [Task 1]\n  1003\t- A truthful partial implementation does not satisfy an acceptance contract: SFN-21 remained NO-GO for unavailable modules, incomplete SDK, audit recovery, key-name-wide secret allowlisting, and MailFn credential rotation. [Task 2]\n  1004\t- The root README is incomplete for admin inventory: inspect tracked `*fn` packages. Stateful/control-plane products such as AuthFn, BillFn, DataFn, FileFn, PlugFn, MailFn/SendFn, FlowFn, HostFn, WatchFn/LogFn, SecFn, SearchFn, CmsFn/ContentFn, CompFn, CiFn, RecFn, UserFn, MemoryFn, and TestFn need operator UI; pure libraries/dev UI infrastructure do not. [Task 3]\n  1005\t- For private Superfunctions PR operations, use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`; target `sf-next/next`, include `.conduct` for that target, verify ancestry/changed files/generated artifacts, and read back the exact live PR head. The final SFN-21 contract gate recorded 29 packages, 130 resources, 347 operations and 74/74 tests. [Task 3]\n  1006\t\n  1007\t## Failures and how to do differently\n  1458\t## Reusable knowledge\n  1459\t\n  1460\t- `sf-next/next`, not `origin/next`, is the valid next ref. In private 21n repos, use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other` if default `gh` returns misleading 404. Test caller-supplied `environmentId` where IDs outrank environment scope. [Task 1]\n  1461\t- Package releases require package-local install/build/test/pack and dependency-safe batches. Failed immutable `@plugfn/providers@0.0.1` required corrected `0.0.2`; do not reuse failed tags. [Task 2]\n  1462\t- McpFn release gate needs Node 24; a root install can mask standalone dependencies. In hosted McpFn CI, run `node scripts/ci-install-rollup-native.mjs` after `npm ci` before the gate because npm can omit `@rollup/rollup-linux-x64-gnu`. Validate post-push local/ref/PR SHA equality and merge with an exact-head guard. [Task 2]\n  1463\t- Worktree snapshots are cache-relative without fetch; take final counts after detailed inspection if a checkout changes concurrently. [Task 3]\n  1464\t- For private Superfunctions PRs, inspect authenticated current `reviewThreads`/head comments, including `isResolved` and `isOutdated`, before editing. PR #103 used a clean isolated exact-head worktree because the existing checkout was dirty; after user authorization, fetch `origin/SF-8`, require it to equal `HEAD^`, then push `HEAD:SF-8` and verify local/remote/live PR SHA equality. [Task 4]\n  1465\t\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"   323\tscope: Use for DATA-1/AUTH-1 local-only canonical-gateway implementation behind a hosted approval gate.\n   324\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev; reuse_rule=worktree, approval, and exact-head procedures are reusable, but code, PR, CI, and deployment evidence are snapshot-specific.\n   325\t\n   326\t## Task 1: Implement DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in isolated worktrees, partial\n   327\t\n   328\t### rollout_summary_files\n   329\t\n   330\t- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T04:09:11+00:00, thread_id=01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af, DATA-1 published; AUTH-1 has one unresolved remote FastAPI CI failure)\n   331\t\n   332\t### keywords\n   333\t\n   334\t- DATA-1, AUTH-1, canonical-gateway, origin/dev, 72aabce, placement, CAS, HMAC assertions, replay protection, single-writer-strong, PR #121, PR #120, FastAPI, StopIteration\n   335\t\n   336\t## User preferences\n   337\t\n   338\t- when the user request