{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T06:25:11.092Z","ordinal":12134,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04c30-8e87-7781-bbc7-0acb090224d6","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e2131e76-b02d-4a21-bcde-f0ab56c4de58","process_id":"68030","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md | sed -n '1,90p'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md | sed -n '1,90p'","name":"REDACTED.md","path":"/Users/serro/.codex/memories/rollout_summaries/2026-08-23T17-51-55-LP4P-data1_auth1_implementation_review_merge_worktree_cleanup.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"     1\tthread_id: 01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af\n     2\tupdated_at: 2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00\n     3\trollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl\n     4\tcwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n     5\tgit_branch: SFNS-2\n     6\t\n     7\t# DATA-1 and AUTH-1 were implemented, reviewed, merged, and their dedicated worktrees removed\n     8\t\n     9\tRollout context: The user requested end-to-end work on Linear issues DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in separate worktrees based on freshly fetched `origin/dev`, followed by PR review remediation, merging, and cleanup. The original dirty checkout `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev` was preserved. Hosted Skillplane workflow `21n/work-linear-issue@1.0.1` was retrieved and followed.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Task 1: Implement DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in isolated worktrees\n    12\t\n    13\tOutcome: success\n    14\t\n    15\tPreference signals:\n    16\t- The user asked to “work DATA-1 and AUTH-1 issues in a new worktrees off of origin/dev end to end” -> preserve the existing checkout, use separate clean worktrees from the authoritative fetched ref, and keep issue scopes isolated.\n    17\t- The workflow required local implementation and verification before publication approval, then exact issue-ID branches for publication.\n    18\t\n    19\tKey steps:\n    20\t- Read both complete Linear issues, all comments, linked architecture/rationale documents, relations, and project metadata.\n    21\t- Fetched `origin/dev` at `72aabce915426325450663feffd7a53089ef4489` and created detached worktrees under `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/DATA-1` and `AUTH-1`.\n    22\t- DATA-1 implemented tenant placement separate from permission indexing, atomic placement/CAS epoch moves, gateway dispatch, signed assertions, pre-execution fencing, bounded retry, sync/WebSocket behavior, migration fencing, observability, provider-neutral adapters, tests, and documentation.\n    23\t- AUTH-1 implemented canonical gateway routing with direct-mode compatibility, identity placement/CAS, signed HMAC assertions and replay protection, pre-side-effect routing, TypeScript/Python adapter support, OAuth/session semantics, deletion fencing, migration behavior, Swift/client updates, tests, and documentation.\n    24\t- DATA-1 was published as PR #121 and AUTH-1 as PR #120. DATA-1 later received one narrow remediation fixing placement validation order before custom-route middleware; commit `1bf6f6bb` was pushed and verified against the PR head.\n    25\t\n    26\tFailures and how to do differently:\n    27\t- The original checkout was dirty with unrelated `.conduct` artifacts; do not clean or modify it during similar work.\n    28\t- AUTH-1’s initial remote CI had unrelated repository failures, including a FastAPI `StopIteration` issue in prior history; distinguish local feature validation from repository-wide CI and live multi-region proof.\n    29\t\n    30\tReusable knowledge:\n    31\t- Placement ownership must remain a separate source of truth from permission-grant projections/outboxes.\n    32\t- Routing assertions should bind request identity and relevant method/path/body data, and stale routing may retry only once before execution.\n    33\t- DynamoDB placement used `single-writer-strong` consistency; Global Table replicas are not globally atomic.\n    34\t\n    35\tReferences:\n    36\t- Hosted workflow: `21n/work-linear-issue@1.0.1`, digest prefix `716e55…abaf`.\n    37\t- Worktrees: `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/DATA-1`, `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/AUTH-1`.\n    38\t- DATA-1 PR #121: `https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/121`.\n    39\t- AUTH-1 PR #120: `https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120`.\n    40\t\n    41\t## Task 2: Bounded AUTH-1 PR review remediation\n    42\t\n    43\tOutcome: success\n    44\t\n    45\tPreference signals:\n    46\t- The user invoked `splane pr-refetch-fix AUTH-1` -> use one bounded review round: fetch unresolved GraphQL threads plus reviews, issue comments, inline comments, and checks; classify against the exact PR worktree; push at most once; verify heads once; do not refetch or poll afterward.\n    47\t\n    48\tKey steps:\n    49\t- Confirmed AUTH-1 worktree was clean and local, remote, and PR heads matched `bf3a19d192741f0ef19c676cb37e7713a1794aaa`.\n    50\t- Frozen review snapshot contained 56 threads, 14 unresolved, 10 with current comments, 4 outdated-only threads, 49 reviews, 4 issue comments, 54 inline comments, and 28 checks.\n    51\t- Verified all unresolved findings against current code. Middleware execution, `/runtime` compatibility/global classification, cell-region registration precedence, deletion fencing, error propagation, and related issues were already fixed or stale. No edit, commit, or push was needed.\n    52\t- Recorded unrelated failed CI causes: DevFn required Node 22 but CI used Node 20; BillFn and SQLAlchemy had pre-existing typing issues; python-core had Ruff import formatting failures.\n    53\t\n    54\tFailures and how to do differently:\n    55\t- Do not treat every unresolved GitHub thread as actionable; inspect `isOutdated`, current code, and the exact PR head.\n    56\t- Do not use timestamp-only comment queries; unresolved historical threads can remain actionable, while many current-looking threads are stale.\n    57\t\n    58\tReusable knowledge:\n    59\t- For private GitHub operations use `GH_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/serro/.config/gh-other`.\n    60\t- Use exact-head guards such as `--match-head-commit`; after an authorized push, compare local, remote, and live PR SHAs once and stop.\n    61\t\n    62\tReferences:\n    63\t- Skill: `/Users/serro/.codex/skills/pr-refetch-fix/SKILL.md`.\n    64\t- AUTH-1 final reviewed head: `bf3a19d192741f0ef19c676cb37e7713a1794aaa`.\n    65\t- AUTH-1 PR review result: 0 fixes; all 14 unresolved threads stale/already fixed.\n    66\t\n    67\t## Task 3: Merge AUTH-1 and DATA-1 into dev\n    68\t\n    69\tOutcome: success\n    70\t\n    71\tKey steps:\n    72\t- Confirmed both PRs were clean and mergeable; merge commits were enabled.\n    73\t- Merged AUTH-1 first with an exact-head guard. PR #120 merged at `REDACTED`.\n    74\t- Fetched the resulting `origin/dev` and merged it into DATA-1. Git’s `ort` merge completed without conflicts; no manual conflict resolution was required.\n    75\t- Ran the combined DATA-1 server suite: 92 test files, 1,007 passed, 1 skipped; DataFn typecheck, build, and `git diff --check` passed.\n    76\t- Pushed DATA-1 merge commit `3158fc83f2c072bc0a6225cb9e3350abaef92e0e`, verified local/remote/PR heads, then merged PR #121 at `e3b9834c599fe513fb38dd8154299a76d1162309`.\n    77\t- Verified both PR heads are ancestors of final `origin/dev` `e3b9834c599fe513fb38dd8154299a76d1162309`.\n    78\t\n    79\tFailures and how to do differently:\n    80\t- Refresh a dependent PR against the actual post-merge `origin/dev` before merging it. This avoided guessing about overlap and confirmed whether conflicts existed.\n    81\t\n    82\tReusable knowledge:\n    83\t- Exact merge pattern: inspect PR state/heads, merge first PR with `--match-head-commit`, fetch `origin/dev`, merge into dependent worktree, run focused validation, push once, re-read PR head, merge with exact-head guard, and verify ancestry in `origin/dev`.\n    84\t\n    85\tReferences:\n    86\t- AUTH-1 merge commit: `REDACTED`.\n    87\t- DATA-1 branch merge commit before PR merge: `3158fc83f2c072bc0a6225cb9e3350abaef92e0e`.\n    88\t- Final `origin/dev`: `e3b9834c599fe513fb38dd8154299a76d1162309`.\n    89\t- Validation: `npm --workspace datafn/server test`, `npm --workspace datafn/server run typecheck`, `npm --workspace datafn/server run build`, `git diff --check`.\n    90\t\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"     1\tthread_id: 01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af\n     2\tupdated_at: 2026-08-25T16:25:10+00:00\n     3\trollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T23-21-55-01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af.jsonl\n     4\tcwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n     5\tgit_branch: SFNS-2\n     6\t\n     7\t# DATA-1 and AUTH-1 were implemented, reviewed, merged, and their dedicated worktrees removed\n     8\t\n     9\tRollout context: The user requested end-to-end work on Linear issues DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in separate worktrees based on freshly fetched `origin/dev`, followed by PR review remediation, merging, and cleanup. The original dirty checkout `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev` was preserved. Hosted Skillplane workflow `21n/work-linear-issue@1.0.1` was retrieved and followed.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Task 1: Implement DATA-1 and AUTH-1 in isolated worktrees\n    12\t\n    13\tOutcome: success\n    14\t\n    15\tPreference signals:\n    16\t- The user asked to “work DATA-1 and AUTH-1 issues in a new worktrees off of origin/dev end to end” -> preserve the existing checkout, use separate clean worktrees from the authoritative fetched ref, and keep issue scopes isolated.\n    17\t- The workflow required local implementation and verification before publication approval, then exact issue-ID branches for publication.\n    18\t\n    19\tKey steps:\n    20\t- Read both complete Linear issues, all comments, linked architecture/rationale documents, relations, and project metadata.\n    21\t- Fetched `origin/dev` at `72aabce915426325450663feffd7a53089ef4489` and created detached worktrees under `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/DATA-1` and `AUTH-1`.\n    22\t- DATA-1 implemented tenant placement separate from permission indexing, atomic placement/CAS epoch moves, gateway dispatch, signed assertions, pre-execution fencing, bounded retry, sync/WebSocket behavior, migration fencing, observability, provider-neutral adapters, tests, and documentation.\n    23\t- AUTH-1 implemented canonical gateway routing with direct-mode compatibility, identity placement/CAS, signed HMAC assertions and replay protection, pre-side-effect routing, TypeScript/Python adapter support, OAuth/session semantics, deletion fencing, migration behavior, Swift/client updates, tests, and documentation.\n    24\t- DATA-1 was published as PR #121 and AUTH-1 as PR #120. DATA-1 later received one narrow remediation fixing placement validation order before custom-route middleware; commit `1bf6f6bb` was pushed and verified against the PR head.\n    25\t\n    26\tFailures and how to do differently:\n    27\t- The original checkout was dirty with unrelated `.conduct` artifacts; do not clean or modify it during similar work.\n    28\t- AUTH-1’s initial remote CI had unrelated repository failures, including a FastAPI `StopIteration` issue in prior history; distinguish local feature validation from repository-wide CI and live multi-region proof.\n    29\t\n    30\tReusable knowledge:\n    31\t- Placement ownership must remain a separate source of truth from permission-grant projections/outboxes.\n    32\t- Routing assertions should bind request identity and relevant method/path/body data, and stale routing may retry only once before execution.\n    33\t- DynamoDB placement used `single-writer-strong` consistency; Global Table replicas are not globally atomic.\n    34\t\n    35\tReferences:\n    36\t- Hosted workflow: `21n/work-linear-issue@1.0.1`, digest prefix `716e55…abaf`.\n    37\t- Worktrees: `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/DATA-1`, `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/AUTH-1`.\n    38\t- DATA-1 PR #121: `https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/121`.\n    39\t- AUTH-1 PR #120: `https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/120`.\n    40\t\n    41\t## Task 2: Bounded AUTH-1 PR review remediation\n    42\t\n    43\tOutcome: success\n    44\t\n    45\tPreference signals:\n    46\t- The user invoked `splane pr-refetch-fix AUTH-1` -> use one bounded review round: fetch unresolved GraphQL threads plus reviews, issue comments, inline comments, and checks; classify against the exact PR worktree; push at most once; verify heads once; do not refetch or poll afterward.\n    47\t\n    48\tKey steps:\n    49\t- Confirmed AUTH-1 worktree was clean and local, remote, and PR heads matched `bf3a19d192741f0ef19c676cb37e7713a1794aaa`.\n    50\t- Frozen review snapshot contained 56 threads, 14 unresolved, 10 with current comments, 4 outdated-only threads, 49 reviews, 4 issue comments, 54 inline comments, and 28 checks.\n    51\t- Verified all unresolved findings against current code. Middleware execution, `/runtime` compatibility/global classification, cell-region registration precedence, deletion fencing, error propagation, and related issues were already fixed or stale. No edit, commit, or push was needed.\n    52\t- Recorded unrelated failed CI causes: DevFn required Node 22 but CI used Node 20; BillFn and SQLAlchemy had pre-existing typing issues; python-core had Ruff import formatting failures.\n    53\t\n    54\tFailures and how to do differently:\n    55\t- Do not treat e