{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T06:25:33.575Z","ordinal":12141,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04c30-8e87-7781-bbc7-0acb090224d6","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0eef853664611d0c016a927b5b3f7487d0b2ca612069f12085","summary_text":["**Finalizing shared outcome and Mermaid syntax**","**Refining data sequence and migration state diagrams**","**Detailing auth sequence and lifecycle diagrams**"],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1787984731523,"completed_at_ms":1787984733575}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T06:25:33.579Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0eef853664611d0c016a927b5b3f7487d0b2ca612069f12085","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04c30-8e87-7781-bbc7-0acb090224d6"},"summary":[{"text":"**Finalizing shared outcome and Mermaid syntax**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Refining data sequence and migration state diagrams**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Detailing auth sequence and lifecycle diagrams**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T06:25:46.771Z","ordinal":12143,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04c30-8e87-7781-bbc7-0acb090224d6","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a927b5d6da487d0b84881b760272685","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The common architectural shift was: clients keep one canonical endpoint, while an authoritative placement directory decides which regional cell owns the tenant or identity.\n\n## DATA-1 — tenant data routing\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant C as Client\n    participant G as Canonical DataFn gateway\n    participant P as Placement directory\n    participant R as Regional DataFn cell\n    participant D as Tenant DB / Sync / WebSocket\n\n    C->>G: Request using one remote or wsUrl\n    G->>P: Resolve authenticated namespace\n    P-->>G: active(region, epoch, destination)\n    G->>R: Forward with signed request-bound assertion\n    R->>R: Verify signature, request digest, TTL and nonce\n    R->>P: Re-read authoritative placement\n\n    alt Region and epoch match\n        R->>D: Execute HTTP, REST, sync or WS operation\n        D-->>R: Result\n        R-->>G: Response\n        G-->>C: Response\n    else Stale placement detected before execution\n        R-->>G: Authenticated region mismatch\n        G->>P: Invalidate cache and re-resolve\n        G->>R: Retry exactly once\n    else Moving, tombstoned or ambiguous failure\n        R-->>G: Fail closed; do not replay\n        G-->>C: Retryable or terminal error\n    end\n```\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> SourceActive\n    SourceActive --> Moving: CAS epoch N → N+1<br/>fence writes and WebSockets\n    Moving --> TargetPending: drain permission outbox<br/>copy and validate data<br/>rebuild projection and warm target\n    TargetPending --> TargetActive: CAS N+2<br/>resume target and clear recovery state\n    Moving --> SourceRecovery: failure before activation\n    SourceRecovery --> SourceActive: idempotent rollback<br/>final epoch CAS\n```\n\nKey change: namespace ownership is now separate from the permission-directory projection. Placement uses linearizable reads and CAS epochs; sync, WebSockets, plugin routes and migrations all honor the same pre-execution fence.\n\n## AUTH-1 — identity routing\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant C as Browser / API / OAuth client\n    participant G as Canonical AuthFn gateway\n    participant P as Identity placement directory\n    participant R as Private cell registry\n    participant A as Regional AuthFn cell\n    participant S as Auth DB / OTP / Tokens\n\n    C->>G: Request at canonical authority\n    alt Global discovery or non-enumerating lookup\n        G-->>C: Canonical response without topology signal\n    else Identity-scoped route\n        G->>G: Classify route and derive trusted identity key\n        G->>P: Lookup or approved first-use claim\n        P-->>G: active(region, epoch)\n        G->>R: Resolve opaque cell destination\n        R-->>G: Internal target and audience\n        G->>A: HMAC assertion bound to identity and request\n        A->>A: Verify signature and atomically claim nonce\n        A->>P: Re-read placement before side effects\n\n        alt Region and epoch match\n            A->>S: Authentication, session, OAuth or token work\n            S-->>A: Canonical issuer/cookie/callback result\n            A-->>G: Response\n            G-->>C: Response\n        else Stale placement before side effects\n            A-->>G: Signed mismatch\n            G->>P: Refresh placement\n            G->>A: Retry exactly once\n        else Missing, moving, deleting or tombstoned\n            A-->>G: Fail closed\n            G-->>C: No default-region fallback\n        end\n    end\n```\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> Active\n    Active --> Moving: migration CAS<br/>epoch + 1\n    Moving --> ActiveTarget: copy, validate and warm<br/>epoch + 2\n    Active --> Deleting: fence before account cascade\n    Deleting --> Tombstoned: deletion succeeds\n    Deleting --> Active: deletion fails or operator restores\n```\n\nKey change: AuthFn gained canonical identity placement, replay-resistant HMAC forwarding, epoch validation before any auth side effect, migration and durable account-deletion fencing—while retaining separately configured direct-mode compatibility and canonical OAuth, cookie and issuer behavior.\n\nDetailed references: [DataFn gateway design](/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/datafn/docs/content/docs/documentation/multi-region-gateway.mdx) and [AuthFn canonical-gateway design](/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/authfn/docs/content/docs/recipes/canonical-gateway-multi-region.md).\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"rollout_summaries/2026-08-23T17-51-55-LP4P-data1_auth1_implementation_review_merge_worktree_cleanup.md","lineStart":19,"lineEnd":33,"note":"implementation scope and shared routing invariants"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":740,"lineEnd":745,"note":"placement ownership separation and bounded stale routing"}],"rolloutIds":["01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af"]}},"started_at_ms":1787984733580,"completed_at_ms":1787984746770}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T06:25:46.786Z","ordinal":12144,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a927b5d6da487d0b84881b760272685","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The common architectural shift was: clients keep one canonical endpoint, while an authoritative placement directory decides which regional cell owns the tenant or identity.\n\n## DATA-1 — tenant data routing\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant C as Client\n    participant G as Canonical DataFn gateway\n    participant P as Placement directory\n    participant R as Regional DataFn cell\n    participant D as Tenant DB / Sync / WebSocket\n\n    C->>G: Request using one remote or wsUrl\n    G->>P: Resolve authenticated namespace\n    P-->>G: active(region, epoch, destination)\n    G->>R: Forward with signed request-bound assertion\n    R->>R: Verify signature, request digest, TTL and nonce\n    R->>P: Re-read authoritative placement\n\n    alt Region and epoch match\n        R->>D: Execute HTTP, REST, sync or WS operation\n        D-->>R: Result\n        R-->>G: Response\n        G-->>C: Response\n    else Stale placement detected before execution\n        R-->>G: Authenticated region mismatch\n        G->>P: Invalidate cache and re-resolve\n        G->>R: Retry exactly once\n    else Moving, tombstoned or ambiguous failure\n        R-->>G: Fail closed; do not replay\n        G-->>C: Retryable or terminal error\n    end\n```\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> SourceActive\n    SourceActive --> Moving: CAS epoch N → N+1<br/>fence writes and WebSockets\n    Moving --> TargetPending: drain permission outbox<br/>copy and validate data<br/>rebuild projection and warm target\n    TargetPending --> TargetActive: CAS N+2<br/>resume target and clear recovery state\n    Moving --> SourceRecovery: failure before activation\n    SourceRecovery --> SourceActive: idempotent rollback<br/>final epoch CAS\n```\n\nKey change: namespace ownership is now separate from the permission-directory projection. Placement uses linearizable reads and CAS epochs; sync, WebSockets, plugin routes and migrations all honor the same pre-execution fence.\n\n## AUTH-1 — identity routing\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant C as Browser / API / OAuth client\n    participant G as Canonical AuthFn gateway\n    participant P as Identity placement directory\n    participant R as Private cell registry\n    participant A as Regional AuthFn cell\n    participant S as Auth DB / OTP / Tokens\n\n    C->>G: Request at canonical authority\n    alt Global discovery or non-enumerating lookup\n        G-->>C: Canonical response without topology signal\n    else Identity-scoped route\n        G->>G: Classify route and derive trusted identity key\n        G->>P: Lookup or approved first-use claim\n        P-->>G: active(region, epoch)\n        G->>R: Resolve opaque cell destination\n        R-->>G: Internal target and audience\n        G->>A: HMAC assertion bound to identity and request\n        A->>A: Verify signature and atomically claim nonce\n        A->>P: Re-read placement before side effects\n\n        alt Region and epoch match\n            A->>S: Authentication, session, OAuth or token work\n            S-->>A: Canonical issuer/cookie/callback result\n            A-->>G: Response\n            G-->>C: Response\n        else Stale placement before side effects\n            A-->>G: Signed mismatch\n            G->>P: Refresh placement\n            G->>A: Retry exactly once\n        else Missing, moving, deleting or tombstoned\n            A-->>G: Fail closed\n            G-->>C: No default-region fallback\n        end\n    end\n```\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> Active\n    Active --> Moving: migration CAS<br/>epoch + 1\n    Moving --> ActiveTarget: copy, validate and warm<br/>epoch + 2\n    Active --> Deleting: fence before account cascade\n    Deleting --> Tombstoned: deletion succeeds\n    Deleting --> Active: deletion fails or operator restores\n```\n\nKey change: AuthFn gained canonical identity placement, replay-resistant HMAC forwarding, epoch validation before any auth side effect, migration and durable account-deletion fencing—while retaining separately configured direct-mode compatibility and canonical OAuth, cookie and issuer behavior.\n\nDetailed references: [DataFn gateway design](/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/datafn/docs/content/docs/documentation/multi-region-gateway.mdx) and [AuthFn canonical-gateway design](/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev/authfn/docs/content/docs/recipes/canonical-gateway-multi-region.md).\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nrollout_summaries/REDACTED.md:19-33|note=[implementation scope and shared routing invariants]\nMEMORY.md:740-745|note=[placement ownership separation and bounded stale routing]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04c30-8e87-7781-bbc7-0acb090224d6","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
