{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:06.980Z","ordinal":12175,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a04d77-6b24-7752-b2d1-1391f807b2c2","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"does the server code still gets executed near the db?\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203","create_time":1788006066.980153,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:06.980Z","ordinal":12176,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203","item":{"type":"UserMessage","id":"01a04d77-6b24-7752-b2d1-13a436ed37d4","client_id":"6f1c17d3-47c0-4332-95b2-88299ad93612","content":[{"type":"text","text":"does the server code still gets executed near the db?\n","text_elements":[]}]},"started_at_ms":1788006066980,"completed_at_ms":1788006066980}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:11.389Z","ordinal":12177,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0eef853664611d0c016a92ceb4dc0887d0a22bafac4914c6cb","summary_text":[],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1788006068930,"completed_at_ms":1788006071389}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:11.393Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0eef853664611d0c016a92ceb4dc0887d0a22bafac4914c6cb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:14.580Z","ordinal":12179,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a92ceb751f887d08906489d3e1d62a8","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes. The actual business/server code still executes in the regional cell beside its database.\n\n```text\nClient\n  ↓\nCanonical gateway — only chooses the region\n  ↓\nRegional DataFn/AuthFn server — runs the request\n  ↓\nRegional database\n```\n\nFor example, if Acme’s data lives in Europe:\n\n```text\nClient in India\n  → canonical gateway\n  → European DataFn server\n  → European database\n```\n\nThe gateway does not perform database queries, authentication mutations, token issuance, sync writes, and so on. It only:\n\n- Looks up the owning region.\n- Signs and forwards the request.\n- Retries once if the placement recently changed.\n\nThe regional server verifies ownership immediately before executing the operation.\n\nOne caveat: the code enables this architecture, but “near the DB” still depends on deployment configuration—the regional server and database must actually be deployed in the same region/network. AuthFn’s genuinely global endpoints, such as discovery, may finish at the gateway without contacting a regional database."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1788006071396,"completed_at_ms":1788006074580}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:14.583Z","ordinal":12180,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a92ceb751f887d08906489d3e1d62a8","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Yes. The actual business/server code still executes in the regional cell beside its database.\n\n```text\nClient\n  ↓\nCanonical gateway — only chooses the region\n  ↓\nRegional DataFn/AuthFn server — runs the request\n  ↓\nRegional database\n```\n\nFor example, if Acme’s data lives in Europe:\n\n```text\nClient in India\n  → canonical gateway\n  → European DataFn server\n  → European database\n```\n\nThe gateway does not perform database queries, authentication mutations, token issuance, sync writes, and so on. It only:\n\n- Looks up the owning region.\n- Signs and forwards the request.\n- Retries once if the placement recently changed.\n\nThe regional server verifies ownership immediately before executing the operation.\n\nOne caveat: the code enables this architecture, but “near the DB” still depends on deployment configuration—the regional server and database must actually be deployed in the same region/network. AuthFn’s genuinely global endpoints, such as discovery, may finish at the gateway without contacting a regional database."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:14.699Z","ordinal":12181,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":341574,"cached_input_tokens":239872,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2939,"reasoning_output_tokens":1706,"total_tokens":344513},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":117569,"cached_input_tokens":114432,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":363,"reasoning_output_tokens":147,"total_tokens":117932},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":44.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1788456712},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"pro","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:21:14.705Z","ordinal":12182,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"01a04d77-6966-7201-a7b1-ac7f76658203","last_agent_message":"Yes. The actual business/server code still executes in the regional cell beside its database.\n\n```text\nClient\n  ↓\nCanonical gateway — only chooses the region\n  ↓\nRegional DataFn/AuthFn server — runs the request\n  ↓\nRegional database\n```\n\nFor example, if Acme’s data lives in Europe:\n\n```text\nClient in India\n  → canonical gateway\n  → European DataFn server\n  → European database\n```\n\nThe gateway does not perform database queries, authentication mutations, token issuance, sync writes, and so on. It only:\n\n- Looks up the owning region.\n- Signs and forwards the request.\n- Retries once if the placement recently changed.\n\nThe regional server verifies ownership immediately before executing the operation.\n\nOne caveat: the code enables this architecture, but “near the DB” still depends on deployment configuration—the regional server and database must actually be deployed in the same region/network. AuthFn’s genuinely global endpoints, such as discovery, may finish at the gateway without contacting a regional database.","started_at":1788006066,"completed_at":1788006074,"duration_ms":8162,"time_to_first_token_ms":4853}}
