{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:22:19.738Z","ordinal":12190,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a92cefb4b9487d0ad813d4efbfcb6bb","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’ll check FileFn’s current upload/storage architecture and separate what already works from what would need a new FileFn-specific placement layer. The DataFn/AuthFn pattern is reusable, but the upload path has a few extra constraints."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788006139407,"completed_at_ms":1788006139738}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:22:19.741Z","ordinal":12191,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a92cefb4b9487d0ad813d4efbfcb6bb","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’ll check FileFn’s current upload/storage architecture and separate what already works from what would need a new FileFn-specific placement layer. The DataFn/AuthFn pattern is reusable, but the upload path has a few extra constraints."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:22:21.407Z","ordinal":12192,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0eef853664611d0c016a92cefbaa8887d0879f84f86ec735b6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_fInTCavkDEABWv0A2JJFSg5I","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd:\"set -e\\nrg -n \\\"FileFn|filefn|signed upload|presign|presigned|multi-region|region|placement|upload\\\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -100\\nrg -n \\\"presign|presigned|signed|upload|region|storage|multipart|gateway|placement\\\" filefn --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' | head -320\\nrg --files filefn | head -180\",\n  workdir:\"/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\",\n  yield_time_ms:10000,\n  max_output_tokens:30000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","create_time":1788006135.177374}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:22:21.507Z","ordinal":12193,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e1525df0-add0-485c-ac5a-64f587c0e15e","process_id":"45303","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","set -e\nrg -n \"FileFn|filefn|signed upload|presign|presigned|multi-region|region|placement|upload\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -100\nrg -n \"presign|presigned|signed|upload|region|storage|multipart|gateway|placement\" filefn --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' | head -320\nrg --files filefn | head -180"],"cwd":"file:///Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"set -e\nrg -n \"FileFn|filefn|signed upload|presign|presigned|multi-region|region|placement|upload\" /Users/serro/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -100\nrg -n \"presign|presigned|signed|upload|region|storage|multipart|gateway|placement\" filefn --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**' | head -320\nrg --files filefn | head -180"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"600:# Task Group: August 23 Skillplane PR stacks, bounded review, and multi-region audit\n601:scope: Use for GitHub-native Skillplane stacked PR status, hosted bounded review-fix rounds, or read-only multi-region architecture analysis.\n624:## Task 3: Audit Skillplane multi-region architecture read-only, success\n628:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/agent/experiments/skillplane, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/08/23/rollout-2026-08-23T22-10-13-01a02f7e-7c4f-7941-9a73-463779dc38ff.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-23T16:52:53+00:00, thread_id=01a02f7e-7c4f-7941-9a73-463779dc38ff, static architecture guidance; no implementation/tests)\n632:- multi-region, global control plane, regional single-writer workspace cells, workspace_id, routing_epoch, WORKSPACE_REGION_MISMATCH, Hyperdrive, R2 residency, Nucleus\n646:- Skillplane’s recommended target is central AuthFn/OAuth/workspace-directory authorization followed by `workspace_id -> region_id/routing_epoch`, a short-lived internal assertion, and private Service Binding forwarding to regional single-writer workspace cells. Reject stale routes with `409 WORKSPACE_REGION_MISMATCH` before side effects. [Task 3]\n652:- Nucleus’s user-home-region implementation is a pattern library, not a deployable drop-in: Skillplane identities can access multiple workspace regions, and R2 location hints are not Indian-residency guarantees. [Task 3]\n772:- DATA-1, AUTH-1, canonical-gateway, origin/dev, 72aabce, placement, CAS, HMAC assertions, replay protection, single-writer-strong, PR #121, PR #120, 1bf6f6bb\n812:- DATA-1 PR #121 and AUTH-1 PR #120 were merged into `dev`; placement ownership remains separate from permission-grant projections/outboxes, while AUTH-1 keeps direct-mode compatibility alongside canonical gateway routing. [Task 1][Task 3]\n813:- DynamoDB placement uses `single-writer-strong` consistency and consistent reads; Global Table replicas are not globally atomic. Routing assertions bind identity plus relevant method/path/body data; stale routing may retry only once before execution. [Task 1]\n819:- Preserve unrelated dirty `.conduct` files in the original checkout; do not clean or modify it. Treat remote repository-wide CI separately from feature-local verification, and do not call live multi-region behavior proven by local success. [Task 1]\n966:- Symptom: Daily Contem generator fails at a brittle `previousCss.replace`, or required-text validation double-encodes `&amp;`. Fix: use a simple stable replacement and escape titles only during HTML rendering (or normalize entities in the validator). [Task 8]\n1141:- when the user clarified “not control plane panel” while asking to increase heading/CTA spacing -> change only the intro region and preserve panel spacing. [Task 1]\n1445:- The root README is incomplete for admin inventory: inspect tracked `*fn` packages. Stateful/control-plane products such as AuthFn, BillFn, DataFn, FileFn, PlugFn, MailFn/SendFn, FlowFn, HostFn, WatchFn/LogFn, SecFn, SearchFn, CmsFn/ContentFn, CompFn, CiFn, RecFn, UserFn, MemoryFn, and TestFn need operator UI; pure libraries/dev UI infrastructure do not. [Task 3]\n2071:- For Superfunctions admin inventory, inspect tracked `*fn` packages directly because the root README is incomplete. `uifn/sf` has backed panels for AuthFn, PlugFn, FileFn, and BillFn; re-inventory tracked `*fn` directories before relying on the 35-product snapshot. [Task 6]\n2198:- Passing alias-collapse tests do not prove replacement/removal safety: explicitly test prefixed -> bare Drive IDs and the inverse. Make historical dedupe durable in every writer before claiming duplicates cannot return. [Task 1]\n2224:- After Worker replacement, purge Cloudflare cache and verify `/`, deep, unknown, and white-paper paths redirect exactly while expected 21n.co routes return 200 and unknown routes 404. [Task 1]\n2351:- Symptom: packaging/install is mistaken for an Open VSX release. Fix: do not claim listing/Cursor marketplace availability until Eclipse authentication, Publisher Agreement, namespace, token, upload, and public API verification succeed. The current blocker requires authorization before contacting Eclipse support. [Task 1]\n2666:- Passing focused tests does not prove multi-region adapters, RLS, or consumer integrations are current; preserve exact failures such as `TS2724` and stale regressions as unresolved validation limits. [Task 2]\n2976:- Public JSON input needs runtime validation before `.trim()`, and async invitation results need a live region; review parent layout (`h-screen`/`overflow-hidden`) for mobile reachability. [Task 2]\n3105:- Symptom: large Product Hunt or archive workflows time out, or an external page fails. Fix: reconnect to the same `Ar@fyweb` Chrome profile, resume durable checkpoints in short batches, and preserve exact source-state failure notes; never invent a replacement URL or external content. [Task 3]\n3637:- For SKI-6, `pnpm mcpfn:verify`, `pnpm test:mcp:contract`, and `pnpm test:mcp:conformance` are the actual Skillplane commands; local/remote McpFn release gates, Auth 57/57, Inspector 6/6, Skillplane contract 8/8, and authenticated conformance 1/1 passed. Draft PR #7 still uses local `link:` dependencies, and exact published-package replacement, controlled Claude/ChatGPT flows, deployment proof, and the late marker edge case remain pending. [Task 12]\n3777:- Use R2 for immutable/binary artifacts, KV for hot latest pointers, Postgres for domains/jobs/versions/provenance/indexes/state, and Hyperdrive for pooled Worker-to-Postgres connectivity. Public reads are `KV -> R2`; KV miss/admin/search is `Hyperdrive -> Postgres -> R2`; publication is `R2 upload -> Postgres transaction -> KV pointer update`. [Task 1][Task 2]\n4019:- superfunctions-dev, Nucleus, AuthFn, DataFn, SearchFn, FileFn, file: dependencies, symlinked-local-packages, root-source-fix, .conduct, 377 files changed\n4030:- Exponential e0, Pagerrr, and Skillplane evidence did not directly attribute the stack to those projects; broad AuthFn modularization is strongly inferred from Nucleus, while SearchFn/FileFn/observability provenance remains unresolved. [Task 1]\n4103:- Symptom: increasing form fixed height still clips metadata. Fix: place spacing inside the relevant form section and size the metadata region for its actual state. [Task 1]\n4221:- when the user said \"yes\" to Storybook, \"borrow concepts only\" for Bit, and \"default\" for the phase-one Superfunction panels -> use Storybook as the workbench surface, Bit as inspiration only, and backed panels as authfn/plugfn/filefn/billfn by default. [Task 1][Task 2]\n5592:# Task Group: DataFn/FileFn transport auth comparison in /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n5593:scope: Use for read-only source comparisons between Nucleus DataFn transport auth and FileFn client auth in `/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev`, especially when the user asks whether FileFn can adopt the same shared HTTP/auth provider shape. Boundaries: this is grounded in current source, not a shipped FileFn API change; re-check the exact client types and request paths before reusing implementation claims.\n5596:## Task 1: Compare current Nucleus DataFn transport auth against FileFn demo auth, success\n5600:- rollout_summaries/2026-06-24T06-32-02-7DtI-datafn_filefn_auth_transport_comparison.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/06/24/rollout-2026-06-24T12-02-03-019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56.jsonl, updated_at=2026-06-24T06:37:57+00:00, thread_id=019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56, exact call-site read separated AuthFn-backed DataFn transport auth from FileFn’s simpler `getAuthHeaders` demo)\n5604:- datafn.store.ts, createNucleumDatafnHttpOptions, createNucleumAuthFnTransportAuth, shouldUseAuthFnBearerSession, filefn, getAuthHeaders, +page.svelte\n5606:## Task 2: Judge whether FileFn can accept the same shared transport/auth shape, success\n5610:- rollout_summaries/2026-06-24T06-32-02-7DtI-datafn_filefn_auth_transport_comparison.md (cwd=/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev, rollout_path=/Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/06/24/rollout-2026-06-24T12-02-03-019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56.jsonl, updated_at=2026-06-24T06:37:57+00:00, thread_id=019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56, verified that the shared `@superfunctions/http` auth provider already exists and FileFn could align to it with caveats)\n5614:- HttpTransportAuthProvider, packages/http/src/types.ts, datafn/client/src/transport/http.ts, authfn createTransportAuth, filefn/client/src/client.ts, presigned upload\n5625:- FileFn’s current example client exposes only `getAuthHeaders` and merges those headers manually; it does not yet accept the shared transport-auth provider directly. [Task 1]\n5626:- FileFn already centralizes most API calls through `request()`, so it could accept the same shared `@superfunctions/http` transport auth shape by plumbing an `auth` option through that helper while keeping `getAuthHeaders` as a compatibility alias. [Task 2]\n5627:- Presigned upload URL `PUT` requests are intentionally separate from FileFn API requests and should not automatically inherit the same app auth headers/provider. [Task 1][Task 2]\n5632:- Symptom: a comparison answer implies all FileFn network calls can share one auth object. Cause: presigned upload fetches were collapsed into the main API request path. Fix: keep API-request auth and signed-URL upload auth as separate paths. [Task 1][Task 2]\n5646:- account-service, DataFn, AuthFn, verification matrix, services/account/src/testing/datafn-smoke.ts, test:e2e:apifn:memory, test:e2e:apifn:multiregion, test:e2e:apifn:ratelimit, worker:build, observability, x-account, x-datafn-region\n5656:- The best account-service E2E entrypoints for this family are `services/account/src/testing/run-apifn-memory.ts`, `run-apifn-multiregion.ts`, and `run-apifn-ratelimit.ts`, exposed through `services/account/package.json` as `test:e2e:apifn:memory`, `test:e2e:apifn:multiregion`, and `test:e2e:apifn:ratelimit`. [Task 1]\n5658:- `services/account/src/http/observability.ts` is the key file for `server-timing`, `x-account-*` headers, and redacted request logging, while `services/account/src/datafn/server.ts` owns `x-datafn-region`, public links, search, and rate-limit wiring. [Task 1]\n5659:- Shared-package regression anchors already exist in `packages/observability/src/index.test.ts`, `datafn/server/__tests__/observability-events.test.ts`, `datafn/server/__tests__/rate-limit.test.ts`, `authfn/core/src/__tests__/integration-browser.test.ts`, `authfn/core/src/__tests__/rate-limit.test.ts`, and `authfn/core/src/__tests__/multi-region.test.ts`. [Task 1]\n6190:- Symptom: a product page is deleted or 404s and exposes no official `Visit website` URL. Cause: the source page itself no longer provides the outbound link, so the missing URL is a source-state fact. Fix: preserve `websiteUrl: null`, keep the Product Hunt URL plus the deleted-listing caveat, and do not guess a replacement domain. [Task 2]\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:5:  uploadFile(input: {\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:22:  onSyncError?: (error: Error, uploadSessionId: string) => void;\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:103:   * Register a listener for a specific upload session completion.\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:105:  waitForUpload(uploadSessionId: string): Promise<{ fileId: string; versionId: string }> {\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:106:    const settled = this.settledResults.get(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:115:      if (!this.listeners.has(uploadSessionId)) {\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:116:        this.listeners.set(uploadSessionId, []);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:118:      this.listeners.get(uploadSessionId)!.push((result) => {\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:128:  private notifyListeners(uploadSessionId: string, result: { fileId: string; versionId: string } | Error) {\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:129:    this.clearRetry(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:130:    this.clearSettledResult(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:131:    this.settledResults.set(uploadSessionId, result);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:133:      this.clearSettledResult(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:134:      this.settledResults.delete(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:136:    this.settledResultTimers.set(uploadSessionId, expiry);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:137:    const listeners = this.listeners.get(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:140:      this.listeners.delete(uploadSessionId);\nfilefn/client/src/offline/sync.ts:145:   * Sync 