request helper.\n    60\t- FileFn should keep the existing `getAuthHeaders` path as a compatibility alias if the API is expanded.\n    61\t- AuthFn’s `createTransportAuth()` is the exact factory shape that can feed that shared transport auth contract.\n    62\t- Presigned upload PUTs in FileFn are intentionally separate from API requests; any AuthFn transport integration should apply to FileFn API requests, not blindly to third-party signed URLs.\n    63\t\n    64\tReferences:\n    65\t- [1] `packages/http/src/types.ts:59-87` proves the shared transport auth provider API already exists (`getRequestHeaders`, `getCredentials`, `onUnauthorized`).\n    66\t- [2] `datafn/client/src/transport/http.ts:13-18,147-163` proves DataFn already accepts that shared `auth` provider and merges headers/credentials centrally.\n    67\t- [3] `authfn/client/src/types.ts:174-175` proves AuthFn clients already expose `createTransportAuth(...)`.\n    68\t- [4] `authfn/client/src/regional-client.ts:180-182` proves regional AuthFn clients forward `createTransportAuth(input)` from the underlying client.\n    69\t- [5] `filefn/client/src/client.ts:302-405` proves FileFn has two distinct fetch paths: authenticated API requests through `request()` and presigned URL uploads via raw `fetch()`.\n    70\t- [6] `filefn/client/src/client.ts:390-405` proves the signed-URL PUT path bypasses the main request/auth helper and therefore needs special handling if auth plumbing is added.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3334},"formatted_output":"     1\tthread_id: 019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56\n     2\tupdated_at: 2026-06-24T06:37:57+00:00\n     3\trollout_path: /Users/serro/.codex/sessions/2026/06/24/rollout-2026-06-24T12-02-03-019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56.jsonl\n     4\tcwd: /Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/superfunctions-dev\n     5\tgit_branch: dev\n     6\t\n     7\t# Read-only source comparison of auth handling in Nucleus DataFn vs FileFn\n     8\t\n     9\tRollout context: The u