{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:23:07.982Z","ordinal":12216,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0eef853664611d0c016a92cf20887087d0917171b9085eff55","summary_text":["**Clarifying current citation capabilities**","**Documenting file upload architecture and limitations**"],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1788006176612,"completed_at_ms":1788006187982}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:23:07.985Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0eef853664611d0c016a92cf20887087d0917171b9085eff55","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403"},"summary":[{"text":"**Clarifying current citation capabilities**","type":"summary_text"},{"text":"**Documenting file upload architecture and limitations**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:23:13.881Z","ordinal":12218,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a02fc0-218b-7e61-a134-da5cc89b60af","turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a92cf2be7e087d0a11e391eb928dc05","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes—as a future architecture, this fits FileFn very well. But FileFn is not wired into the new placement/gateway system today.\n\nFileFn already supports multipart signed uploads. What is missing is the multi-region placement and routing layer.\n\n```text\n1. Client → one public FileFn URL\n\n2. Gateway asks:\n   “Which region owns this tenant?”\n\n3. Gateway → regional FileFn server\n\n4. Regional FileFn server:\n   - runs beside the regional metadata DB\n   - creates an upload session\n   - asks the regional object store for a signed upload URL\n\n5. Client → uploads bytes directly to regional object storage\n\n6. Client → public FileFn URL → regional server\n   to confirm and complete the upload\n```\n\nVisually:\n\n```text\n                               ┌→ EU FileFn server → EU metadata DB\nClient → FileFn gateway → directory\n                               └→ India FileFn server → India metadata DB\n                                         │\n                                         ↓\n                                  Regional object store\n                                         ↑\n                              direct signed upload from client\n```\n\nThe important part is that there are two different signatures:\n\n- **Gateway assertion:** proves the regional FileFn server received the request from the trusted gateway for the correct tenant and region.\n- **Signed upload URL:** allows the client to upload one specific file part directly to storage for a limited time.\n\nThey should remain separate. App authentication headers must not be copied onto the storage upload request.\n\nWhat we would need to add to FileFn:\n\n- A `tenant → region + epoch` placement directory.\n- A canonical FileFn gateway.\n- Placement checks before creating, signing or completing upload sessions.\n- Store the owning region and epoch on every upload session.\n- Regional storage targets/buckets selected from trusted placement—not client input.\n- Migration rules that pause new uploads and drain or abort unfinished multipart uploads.\n- Regional processing workers for thumbnails, OCR, video processing and other artifacts.\n- Similar routing for downloads and signed download URLs.\n\nCurrent FileFn already has useful foundations:\n\n- Upload sessions and resumable multipart uploads.\n- Direct-to-storage signed URLs.\n- Proxy upload fallback.\n- Policy-selected storage targets.\n- Separate metadata database and storage adapters.\n- Idempotent upload completion.\n\nSo the answer is: **the design transfers cleanly, and signed uploads are already halfway there—but FileFn still needs its own placement, fencing and canonical-gateway implementation.**\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":5621,"lineEnd":5632,"note":"separation between FileFn API auth and signed storage uploads"},{"path":"rollout_summaries/2026-06-24T06-32-02-7DtI-datafn_filefn_auth_transport_comparison.md","lineStart":50,"lineEnd":69,"note":"verified current FileFn request and presigned upload paths"}],"rolloutIds":["019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56"]}},"started_at_ms":1788006187986,"completed_at_ms":1788006193881}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T12:23:13.883Z","ordinal":12219,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0eef853664611d0c016a92cf2be7e087d0a11e391eb928dc05","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Yes—as a future architecture, this fits FileFn very well. But FileFn is not wired into the new placement/gateway system today.\n\nFileFn already supports multipart signed uploads. What is missing is the multi-region placement and routing layer.\n\n```text\n1. Client → one public FileFn URL\n\n2. Gateway asks:\n   “Which region owns this tenant?”\n\n3. Gateway → regional FileFn server\n\n4. Regional FileFn server:\n   - runs beside the regional metadata DB\n   - creates an upload session\n   - asks the regional object store for a signed upload URL\n\n5. Client → uploads bytes directly to regional object storage\n\n6. Client → public FileFn URL → regional server\n   to confirm and complete the upload\n```\n\nVisually:\n\n```text\n                               ┌→ EU FileFn server → EU metadata DB\nClient → FileFn gateway → directory\n                               └→ India FileFn server → India metadata DB\n                                         │\n                                         ↓\n                                  Regional object store\n                                         ↑\n                              direct signed upload from client\n```\n\nThe important part is that there are two different signatures:\n\n- **Gateway assertion:** proves the regional FileFn server received the request from the trusted gateway for the correct tenant and region.\n- **Signed upload URL:** allows the client to upload one specific file part directly to storage for a limited time.\n\nThey should remain separate. App authentication headers must not be copied onto the storage upload request.\n\nWhat we would need to add to FileFn:\n\n- A `tenant → region + epoch` placement directory.\n- A canonical FileFn gateway.\n- Placement checks before creating, signing or completing upload sessions.\n- Store the owning region and epoch on every upload session.\n- Regional storage targets/buckets selected from trusted placement—not client input.\n- Migration rules that pause new uploads and drain or abort unfinished multipart uploads.\n- Regional processing workers for thumbnails, OCR, video processing and other artifacts.\n- Similar routing for downloads and signed download URLs.\n\nCurrent FileFn already has useful foundations:\n\n- Upload sessions and resumable multipart uploads.\n- Direct-to-storage signed URLs.\n- Proxy upload fallback.\n- Policy-selected storage targets.\n- Separate metadata database and storage adapters.\n- Idempotent upload completion.\n\nSo the answer is: **the design transfers cleanly, and signed uploads are already halfway there—but FileFn still needs its own placement, fencing and canonical-gateway implementation.**\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:5621-5632|note=[separation between FileFn API auth and signed storage uploads]\nrollout_summaries/2026-06-24T06-32-02-7DtI-datafn_filefn_auth_transport_comparison.md:50-69|note=[verified current FileFn request and presigned upload paths]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n019ef854-1ea0-7d31-90cb-fed7430b6a56\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04d78-7145-7893-8452-63cdfa1be403","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
